  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe scallop law's reach ceiling (#37), decided and documented. The generator half is built.\n\n- The scan (`sim/stock_sim/ridge.rs`) looks only within band + 3·tol of the passes, so on flat ground it sees a cusp only up to about 4·tol past the ball (s ≈ 2.9 on an r3 ball at tol 0.1). A stepover of 4 left a 0.606 mm cusp that verified clean. The \"missing-pass law\" the comments relied on doesn't exist.\n- **Built:** `finishing3d::params::scallop_ceiling`, called from the shared `validate`, refuses by name (\"the scallop ceiling\"):\n  - a stated `stepover` or `steep_stepover` at or past the ball diameter, where h = r − √(r² − (s/2)²) stops describing a cusp;\n  - a tolerance at or past r/2, where the automatic stepover √(8·r·tol) reaches 2r.\n  It's a refusal rather than a clamp, so the generator never uses a number the user didn't give.\n- **Not built:** a wider second scan read flat rasters exactly up to s = 5.9, but falsely flagged crowns and corners in 11 finish3d verdict fixtures, so it was reverted. The reach's valid range is documented in `ridge::reach`; the follow-up is #212.\n- One test changed: `the_authored_ladder_spaces_the_rings_and_says_nothing_elsewhere` had steep stepover 8 on a 6 mm ball, now 5.\n\n## Pins (`crates/motion/tests/scallop_ceiling.rs`, 4)\n\nStepover and steep stepover at, just past and well past the diameter are refused; just under generates. Tolerance at and past r/2 is refused; just under generates. Degenerate diameters, tolerances and stepovers are refused by name.\n\n## Readings\n\n- **Release:** finish3d 88/88 (heavy lane included), flow 15, scallop_ceiling 4.\n- **Debug:** ridge_rest 4.\n- **App suites that use 3D finishing, after merging main:** area_controls, center_cut_multiaxis, golden_cl, operations, posed_contact, project_roundtrip, ribbon, tool_gate, tool_law, verify, posting. All green.\n- **Clippy:** clean on motion and sim.\n\nChangelog: 3D finish refuses a stated stepover or steep stepover at or past the ball diameter, and a tolerance at or past half the ball radius, by name (\"the scallop ceiling\"), instead of generating a path whose cusp verified silently\n\nFixes #37\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
